      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T08:15:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "generally we prefer check condition and return early to reduce code nesting\n\nInstead of \n\n```\nif (condition1) {\n  // do 1\n} else if (condition 2) {\n  // do 2\n  if (subcondition2_1) {\n    // do 2_1\n  }\n} else {\n  // do 3\n}\n```\n\nIt is preferred to do\n\n```\nif (condition1) {\n  // do 1\n  return;\n}\n\nif (condition2) {\n  // do 2\n  if (!subcondition2_1) {\n    return;\n  }\n  return;\n}\n\n// do 3\nreturn;\n```\n\nOf course, this pattern does NOT apply if you have comment logic for condition 1, 2, and 3 such as\n\n```\nif (condition1) {\n  // do 1\n} else if (condition 2) {\n  // do 2\n  if (subcondition2_1) {\n    // do 2_1\n  }\n  // do 2_common\n} else {\n  // do 3\n}\n// do common\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1245,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1245,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "72b1174a4f314f73f2c9c0efee2434fb8ebeba0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
